- C. The Clifford algebra of diracForm
- D. The homomorphism ofCliffordAlgebra
  - D.1. Definition and values on the generators
  - D.2. Surjectivity
  - D.3. The dimension of diracAlgebra
  - D.4. Injectivity and the isomorphism

## iv. References

* Dreiner, Haber and Martin, Two-component spinor techniques and Feynman rules for quantum
  field theory and supersymmetry, Phys. Rept. 494 (2010) 1-196. [ref: Dreiner:2008tw]
  The products of gamma matrices with increasing indices are linearly independent:
  Appendix G.3, page 213 of arXiv:0812.1594v6. The case of four dimensions: eq. (G.1.102)
  and footnote 129, page 207.

-/

@[expose] public section
namespace spaceTime
open Complex Fermion.Dirac

noncomputable section diracRepresentation

